  "_doc": "Rest Frame (everyday physics), 'precise and playful': G mixolydian at 112.5 BPM (a beat is 16 frames, a 16th exactly 4 frames at 30 fps). Bright, dry and a little driven: a short studio room, low pads, and staccato instrument blips ticking in eighths that turn to 16ths once the energy rises (no felt piano: that arrangement is Lumevina's); a sub only once the energy rises past 0.6. Foley is hard and close: knocks, ticks and shutters, never bells. Signature, 'coming to rest': knocks D6, B5, G5 at 0, +12 and +20 frames, each gap 2/3 of the last like a ball with a restitution of 0.67 settling, landing home on G. It plays on the end card (signature) and at the end of every counter.",
